    summary30sEn: 'First discovered in rope-pulling experiments by Max Ringelmann in 1913, Social Loafing shows that as group size increases, individual effort drops dramatically. When people feel their individual contributions cannot be identified, their motivation and energy decrease because accountability is diffused across the collective.',
